                "senderName": "NWS Fort Worth TX",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 3 at 3:25PM CDT until October 3 at 4:15PM CDT by NWS Fort Worth TX",
                "description": "At 325 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms that produced\nbetween 3 and 4 inches of rain this afternoon. Several public reports\nhave been received of flooding along Highway 107.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nTemple, Harker Heights, Belton, McGregor, Nolanville, Morgan's\nPoint Resort, Moody, Mother Neff State Park, Belton Lake, Oglesby,\nWhitson, White Hall, Owl Creek, Meadow Grove, The Grove, Moffat,\nWoodland, Leon Junction and Flat.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nIn hilly terrain there are hundreds of low water crossings which are\npotentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not attempt to cross flooded\nroads. Find an alternate route.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
